nLemmas\u202f1,\u202f2 and\u202f3 together give a complete description of the admissible numbers of sunny lines.\n\n* From Lemma\u202f1 we must have \\(k\\ge \\max\\{0,n-2\\}\\).  \n* Lemma\u202f2 shows that \\(k=n-1\\) is impossible.  \n* Lemma\u202f3 provides explicit constructions for every integer \\(k\\) with  \n\n\\[\n\\max\\{0,n-2\\}\\le k\\le n,\\qquad k\\neq n-1 .\n\\]\n\nTherefore the set of all non\u2011negative integers \\(k\\) for which the required configuration exists is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\;k\\in\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n-2,n\\}\\qquad (n\\ge 3).\\;}\n\\]\n\nThis completes the solution. \u220e"
