---------------------------\n### Conclusion\n\nFor every integer \\(n\\ge 3\\) and every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) we\nhave exhibited \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the two conditions of the\nproblem, with exactly \\(k\\) of them sunny.  Lemma\u202f1 shows that no further\nrestriction on \\(k\\) can arise.  Therefore the set of admissible values of\n\\(k\\) is precisely  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\] \u220e"
