}\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**2. Detailed Solution**\n\nLet  \n\n\\[\nS=\\{(a,b)\\in\\mathbb Z^{2}\\mid a\\ge 1,\\;b\\ge 1,\\;a+b\\le n+1\\},\n\\qquad n\\ge 3 .\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 2.1   Cardinality of \\(S\\)\n\nFor each integer \\(s\\) with \\(2\\le s\\le n+1\\) the equation \\(a+b=s\\) has exactly \\(s-1\\) solutions in positive integers.  \nHence  \n\n\\[\n|S|=\\sum_{s=2}^{n+1}(s-1)=\\frac{n(n+1)}2 . \\tag{2.1}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 2.2   Non\u2011sunny lines contain at most \\(n\\) points of \\(S\\)\n\nA line is **non\u2011sunny** iff it is parallel to one of  \n\n\\[\n\\ell_{h}:\\;y=\\text{const},\\qquad \n\\ell_{v}:\\;x=\\text{const},\\qquad \n\\ell_{d}:\\;x+y=\\text{const}.\n\\]\n\n*Horizontal* \\(y=b\\) with \\(1\\le b\\le n\\) contains the points \\((a,b)\\) where \\(1\\le a\\le n+1-b\\); at most \\(n\\) points.\n\n*Vertical* \\(x=a\\) with \\(1\\le a\\le n\\) contains at most \\(n\\) points.\n\n*Diagonal* \\(x+y=c\\) with \\(2\\le c\\le n+1\\) contains exactly \\(c-1\\le n\\) points.\n\nThus any non\u2011sunny line meets \\(S\\) in at most \\(n\\) points. \\(\\square\\)\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 2.3   Sunny lines of slope\u202f1 and their disjointness\n\nFor an integer \\(c\\) define  \n\n\\[\nL(c):\\;y=x+c . \\tag{2.3.1}\n\\]\n\nThe slope of \\(L(c)\\) equals \\(1\\); therefore \\(L(c)\\) is sunny (it is not parallel to the \\(x\\)-axis, the \\(y\\)-axis nor the line \\(x+y=0\\)).\n\nA point \\((a,b)\\in S\\) lies on \\(L(c)\\) iff \\(a-b=c\\).  \nConsequently, for two distinct integers \\(c\\neq c'\\),\n\n\\[\nL(c)\\cap S\\;\\cap\\;L(c')\\cap S=\\varnothing . \\tag{2.3.2}\n\\]\n\nHence the subsets of \\(S\\) cut out by different lines \\(L(c)\\) are pairwise disjoint.\n\nFor a given \\(c\\) the conditions \\(a-b=c,\\;a\\ge1,\\;b\\ge1