up\\mathcal N .\n\\]\n\nBy construction  \n\n* \\(|\\mathcal L|=k+(n-k)=n\\);  \n* the only sunny lines in \\(\\mathcal L\\) are the \\(k\\) lines \\(L_{i}\\);  \n* every point of \\(S\\) lies on at least one line of \\(\\mathcal L\\);  \n* all lines are distinct (the \\(L_{i}\\) have distinct equations, and the non\u2011sunny lines were chosen with distinct horizontal positions).\n\nThus for the prescribed integer \\(k\\) we have exhibited \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the two conditions of the problem and containing exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 2.8   Exhaustion of admissible values of \\(k\\)\n\nThe construction works for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\).  \nSince among \\(n\\) lines we cannot have more than \\(n\\) sunny ones, no other value of \\(k\\) is possible.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The admissible values of }k\\text{ are }0,1,2,\\dots ,n.}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
